## Summary of changes

### Root cause
`AppIcon` was calling `$ui.showApp()` with updated params, which added a new entry to `openApps` but didn't update the **existing** app that all child components were referencing via their original `tabId`.

### Fixes

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `ui.js` | Added `updateAppParams` mutation that replaces `openApps` with spread (triggering Vue reactivity) while keeping the same `tabId` |
| `AppIcon.vue` | Replaced `watch: { project }` + `showApp` with a computed setter `currentProject` that calls `updateAppParams`. Reads `liveApp` from store to stay reactive |
| `main.ts` | `$app` now reads from `$storex.ui.openApps[tabId]` directly (live store), `$projectId` derives from `$app.params.project_id`, and `$project` derives from `$projectId` — creating a full reactive chain |
